From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] shell: Log Out with a second account, power menu buttons in
 rows

Plinius: greetd shows plinius-greeter's account picker once a session
ends, so logging out is how one switches accounts. The system menu of
the top bar and the power menu offer Log Out when the phone has more
than one account one can log in with (the rule of plinius-greeter: a
user ID between UID_MIN and UID_MAX of /etc/login.defs and a login
shell), counted each time a menu opens, so an account just added in
Settings counts at once. With one account the entries stay hidden; on
the lock screen Log Out is off, like Power Off and Restart.

Log Out goes through gnome-session's end session dialog (normal mode)
instead of logging out at once: open apps close, so it asks first, as
Restart UI does.

The power menu's buttons show icon and label side by side in shorter
rows instead of squares, which leaves room for Log Out as a fourth row
across both columns.
